I've written a two-task session plan in session_plan/ and committed it as 9732ece4. The folder is gitignored, so I had to force-add it.

Task 1 (product, #965): make provider errors show up as failures. Right now, when the provider rejects a call with 400, 401, 403 or 404, yoyo -p exits 0. With --output-format json it writes no JSON at all. Any script or CI step that trusts the exit code reads the failure as a success with an empty answer. The fix is to record the error in the last else branch of the error-handling code in src/prompt.rs, so that three things follow:
• the run exits 1,
• the JSON output carries is_error: true,
• a configured fallback provider actually gets tried.

The task asks the implementer to:
• **Commit early:** save the edit before the long build and test run.
• **Avoid a second error line:** make sure the red error: line is not printed twice.
• **Test at the output:** check what the caller actually receives for 400, 401 and 404.
• **Keep the other cases unchanged:** a successful run, a normal end of stream, context overflow (which should still trigger compaction) and retriable 5xx/429 errors must all behave as before.
• **Prove the tests work:** disable the new line on purpose, watch the tests fail, then restore it.
• **Probe the real binary if cheap:** rerun the local test-server check against the built binary.

Task 2 (evolve, #958): review an unchecked change to the risk ledger. Day 210's change to the risk ledger's "unhittable" count (it now records how many files were examined, not just the count) reached main without anyone reviewing it. The task asks the reviewer to confirm three things:
1. The total is saved in the same place as the count.
2. Older records that lack it show "not recorded" rather than a zero.
3. At least one test builds its input through the real code, instead of typing the answer into the test.

Then it runs the same break-it-and-restore check. Either result is a valid finish: a clean review that closes #958, or a small fix to whatever gap turns up.

One thing I found while planning: Task 2's change can't be viewed as a single commit. The repo is a shallow clone, and the only commit touching those files is the clone's boundary, which shows the entire tree as newly added. The task file tells the reviewer to diff the range 9c222c88..HEAD for the four affected files instead.

